From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SoloLuck ops <releases@sololuck.io>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:33:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] SoloLuck: dedicated per-node block submit connsocks

A solved block is now submitted to every configured bitcoind from its own
thread on a private connsock (own socket + semaphore) built from the config
strings, never the shared getblocktemplate connection; 8 s x 3 attempts per
node, caller bounded to 44 s, returns on first acceptance; preciousblock is
issued by each accepting node.

Proven on regtest: a hung primary node went from 90.7 s to 3 ms, and a
stalled getblocktemplate socket from 119.5 s to 21 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
